### Run these in IntelliJ: open this file and click the green ▶ next to each request.
### Start the app first. The H2 database is empty on every start.

### 1. Create a teacher
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "teacher@hvl.no", "name": "Tina Teacher"}

### 2. Create a student
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "student@hvl.no", "name": "Sam Student"}

### 3. Teacher (id 1) creates a course
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "DAT250", "description": "Software technologies", "semester": "Autumn 2026", "teacherId": 1}

### 4. Invite the student into course 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "student@hvl.no", "role": "STUDENT"}

### 5. List participants of course 1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/enrollments

### 6. List all courses
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses

### 7. Courses the student (id 2) is in
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/2/enrollments

### ---------- Modules and contents (run 1–3 above first) ----------

### 8. Add two modules to course 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/modules
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Week 1: Introduction"}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/modules
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Week 2: Persistence"}

### 9. Module 2 requires module 1
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/modules/2/requires/1

### 10. List the course's modules in order
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1/modules

### 11. Add a page, a quiz, a coding exercise and an assignment to module 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/pages
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Welcome", "body": "# Welcome to DAT250\n![logo](https://example.com/logo.png)"}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/quizzes
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Warm-up quiz", "maxAttempts": 3, "showHints": true, "deadline": "2026-10-30T23:59:00Z"}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/coding-exercises
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Hello Spring", "starterRepositoryUrl": "https://git.app.uib.no/example/hello-spring.git", "groupWork": true}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Hand-in 1", "description": "Upload your report as PDF", "deadline": "2026-10-30T23:59:00Z", "lateSubmissionsAllowed": true, "visibleFrom": "2026-10-26T07:00:00Z"}

### 12. All contents of module 1 (teacher's view)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/contents

### 13. Only currently visible contents (student's view)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/contents?visibleOnly=true

### 14. Reorder module 1's contents (ids must list every item once)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/modules/1/contents/order
Content-Type: application/json

{"ids": [4, 1, 2, 3]}
